<title>SWEDEN: Volvo's executive VP Mohlin resigns.</title>
<headline>Volvo's executive VP Mohlin resigns.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker AB Volvo said on Tuesday its executive vice president Per-Erik Mohlin had resigned to take up a position outside the Volvo group.</p>
<p>Mohlin, who has worked for Volvo since 1985, will leave on October 1 this year.</p>
<p>He was president of Volvo Aero Corp from 1989 to 1993 and president of Volvo Car Corp from 1994-95. He took up his current position as executive vice president and member of the group executive committee in the autumn of 1995.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
